# Amik's runtime state. In THIS folder rather than the repository root,
# so it travels when the folder is copied into another project — an
# ignore rule left behind is a lock file committed on someone else's
# first run.

# Who is working a card right now. Machine-local by definition: a pid
# from another machine means nothing, and a committed lock would tell
# every checkout that a card is being worked forever.
.lock

# Where the board stood when the loop last looked. A cursor, not a
# record — deleting it costs one redundant pass and nothing else.
.seen

# The agent's raw output, when [loop] transcript is on. A transcript is
# every file the agent read, which is exactly what should not be
# committed by default.
runs/

# A card's design pass. Transient by design -- its lifetime is its
# card's -- and TRACKING one puts it on a single branch where every
# other branch cannot see it, which is the whole reason a prototype
# went missing and a branch switcher got proposed to find it.
#
# Nothing in git removes these now, so `edit.discard_prototype` is the
# only mechanism there is and every close path calls it.
prototypes/

# Working notes, not documentation. Parked seeds and an agent-landscape
# survey — neither finished enough to publish nor useless enough to
# delete. Revisit when this repository has a docs story.
/SOMEDAY.md
/RESEARCH.md

# What the last verify said. A cursor, not a record: a result from
# another machine means nothing, and losing it costs one pill reading
# "not run yet" until the next card lands.
.verify
